Boost.System has been header-only since 1.69, and Boost 1.91 ships neither the
library nor a boost_system CMake component, so a REQUIRED find_package naming it
leaves the bots core unconfigurable. Only thread and filesystem are compiled,
which is what this leaves it asking for.

Carried here until the fork drops it upstream; the kit re-applies it after
every pull and says so when it no longer fits.

diff --git a/src/modules/PlayerBots/CMakeLists.txt b/src/modules/PlayerBots/CMakeLists.txt
index 43b5000..1b4cf30 100644
--- a/src/modules/PlayerBots/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/modules/PlayerBots/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -192,21 +192,19 @@ if(WIN32)
   # and two of them, filesystem and thread, are compiled rather than
   # header-only. Windows linked neither, which would have failed at link time
   # once the headers were finally found.
-  find_package(Boost 1.70 REQUIRED COMPONENTS thread filesystem system)
+  find_package(Boost 1.70 REQUIRED COMPONENTS thread filesystem)
   target_link_libraries(${LIBRARY_NAME}
     PRIVATE zlib
     PRIVATE ws2_32
     PRIVATE Boost::thread
     PRIVATE Boost::filesystem
-    PRIVATE Boost::system
   )
 else()
-  find_package(Boost 1.70 REQUIRED COMPONENTS thread filesystem system)
+  find_package(Boost 1.70 REQUIRED COMPONENTS thread filesystem)
   target_link_libraries(${LIBRARY_NAME}
     PRIVATE ZLIB::ZLIB
     PRIVATE Boost::thread
     PRIVATE Boost::filesystem
-    PRIVATE Boost::system
   )
 endif()
 
